    "problem": "Although Arctic sea-ice loss is thought to drive cold mid-latitude winters, the specific physical mechanism that links these phenomena remains a subject of debate and is not fully understood.",
    "method": "This study uses observational composite analyses and climate model experiments to demonstrate how Arctic sea-ice loss enhances upward planetary-wave propagation, subsequently weakening the stratospheric polar vortex and inducing cold mid-latitude winters.",
    "task": "The task is to demonstrate, through observational analyses and model experiments, how Arctic sea-ice loss weakens the stratospheric polar vortex via enhanced upward planetary-scale wave propagation, thereby causing cold winters in mid-latitudes.",
